WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.389
So now let's build out a website. And my

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:04.630
favorite part of the craft framework is

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.030
C, which stands for create. So in this

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.870
step, what we're going to do is to build

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.709
the front end of the website. And when I

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:12.390
say the front end, that's basically the

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.830
design that you see without the

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.749
underlying functionality yet. And we're

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:17.430
going to do this in three steps. And

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.189
these steps, you can actually adapt it

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:20.790
even if you're not building a website.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.470
And let's say you're building a piece of

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.910
software that is different from what

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.670
we're about to tackle. This is pretty

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.990
much the same steps that you can do with

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.669
your cloud code. So, first we'll be

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:31.189
planning out the sections of the

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:33.030
website. Essentially, what goes in the

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.870
platform itself. Then, we're going to

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.190
improve the look of it using a design

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.110
system. And then, finally, I'm going to

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.630
teach you how to make it visually

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.389
stunning so that you can stand out

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:44.470
versus everyone else. So, let's start

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.470
with planning the sections of our

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.310
website first. And for this step and

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.910
generally no matter what build you are

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.670
trying to do, it is almost always good

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.590
to just have Claude do some research for

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.590
you in terms of best practices so that

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.430
you can get a great idea of what to

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.750
include and what not to include in this

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.349
creation that you are building. So for

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:02.869
our website, what I sent, which you can

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:04.710
just get below, is this prompt where

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:05.910
we're saying that we're planning the

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.390
sections for our agency, Agency X. You

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.390
can change that to your own. It's an AI

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.230
solutions agency that builds automations

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.310
and agents for clients. We want Claude

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.910
to research what the best agency and

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.310
service sites to include in 2026 and to

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.310
give us the final section list. You can

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.149
see here also that I'm using this skill

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:24.469
called / HTML to render the final

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:26.230
output. And what this skill does, which

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.670
you'll see in a bit, is it will just

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.910
render the plan in HTML, hypertext

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.590
markup language, which is just a bit

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.270
more visual so that you can get an idea

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.950
of what the sections are that are in

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.109
plan. And you don't necessarily need to

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:38.789
do this. If you completely remove this

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:40.789
line, then Claude will just give you the

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:43.350
plan in text here in the chat window,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.030
which is completely fine as well. So now

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.469
that it's completed that, you can see it

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:48.069
returned back to us this nicely

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:50.310
formatted HTML page that is much easier

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.789
to review. So it came back to us with 12

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:54.550
sections in here. So you of course have

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.389
the hero section, you have the trust

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:58.469
bar, you have a framing of the problem

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:00.630
and then your own solution to it. And if

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.550
I were to advise someone on building out

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.709
their first agency website, this is a

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:07.190
good basis. But remember with AI it's

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.790
actually really good in giving you a lot

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.550
of options and at this point this is

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.150
actually where you can apply your best

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.309
judgment on which particular sections

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:16.550
apply to you or not. So for example if I

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.550
were advising someone who is new to this

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.390
space to build their first agency

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.309
website. I probably won't include all of

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.150
these sections just so that they can get

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.309
started the quickest way possible. So

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:27.910
for instance if you look at this case

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.270
studies with hard numbers that's

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.470
probably something that you don't have

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.949
yet. having an interactive proof like an

00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:35.589
ROI calculator or a live demo agent, you

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:37.750
can just add those separately next time.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.270
And so now to build out this website,

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.949
all you need to do is to ask cloud to do

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:42.550
it. So we're saying here to build the

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.949
actual onepage site for agency X based

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:46.790
on having the hero section, having the

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.630
trust bar and a couple of other sections

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.070
that I picked out, including the

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.910
services and the what we build section,

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.470
as well as pricing, FAQs, and the final

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.630
CTA. So you can see here if you're using

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.790
a default cloud code most likely what

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.550
you will get is something similar to

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.350
this where it is quite generic right but

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.030
at this point don't worry about that yet

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.550
because in the next module we'll be

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.190
applying a design system in order to

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.350
make this look much better. But what's

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.270
important here is for you to just double

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.350
check the copy meaning what it says here

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.869
to make sure that it aligns with what

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:19.030
you want to say and also to quickly just

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.750
check out the buttons are working. And

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.589
also just to quickly review that the

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:25.589
sections like the hero page here, you

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:27.350
have the trust bar in here as well as

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.670
